## Bidirectionality (PASS on new code → BREAK under mutation → RESTORE green)

Behavior 1 — band threshold is the clamp's own floor (bandMode, N=114/115).
  PASS: layout.test.ts "false at N=114, true at N=115" green.
  BREAK: mutate `< LAYOUT.minPitch` → `<=` → N=114 now bands → 2 tests FAIL
    (the threshold test + "significant set empty below threshold").
  RESTORE: revert → 17 passed.

Behavior 2 — significant set includes finding-referenced interior machines.
  PASS: "exact set-union …" + "includes finding-referenced interior machines"
    green; 148 (partial.machine) & 149 (starvedFrom) present, at NO boundary.
  BREAK: delete the starved-machines union members from noteFinding → both the
    exact-set and interior-machine tests FAIL (148/149 vanish).
  RESTORE: revert → 17 passed.

Behavior 3 — Schematic band SSR (ONE band + ×161, NOT 161 ticks).
  PASS: smoke "band mode (N=161)" green.
  BREAK: force `layout.band ?` → `false ?` → N=161 renders ticks → band test FAIL.
  RESTORE: revert → 53 passed.

Behavior 4 — scale floor clamps a very wide plan to MIN_PX_PER_DM.
  PASS: svg-scale "clamps to MIN_PX_PER_DM …" green.
  BREAK: drop `Math.max(fit, MIN_PX_PER_DM)` → `fit` → wide plan falls below
    0.06 → floor test FAIL.
  RESTORE: revert → 5 passed.

Behavior 5 — Blueprint svg attributes churned to explicit px (the enumerated pin).
  PASS: smoke "renders the Smelter ×2 floor plan" green on explicit width/height.
  BREAK: revert `width={w*scale}` → `width="100%"` → the explicit-px pin FAILs.
  RESTORE: revert → 53 passed.

